Subject: [PATCH] pushd: use aes128gcm (RFC 8291) content encoding for web push

The vapid outbound consumer encrypts payloads with the legacy "aesgcm"
draft encoding, whose decryption parameters travel in HTTP headers.
UnifiedPush distributors forward only the request body, so payloads sent
this way cannot be decrypted by UnifiedPush clients. Browsers have
supported the final aes128gcm encoding (where the salt and key are part
of the body) since ~2017, so switching is safe for web clients and
enables Google-free push on Android.

--- a/crates/daemons/pushd/src/consumers/outbound/vapid.rs
+++ b/crates/daemons/pushd/src/consumers/outbound/vapid.rs
@@
-        builder.set_payload(ContentEncoding::AesGcm, payload_body.as_bytes());
+        builder.set_payload(ContentEncoding::Aes128Gcm, payload_body.as_bytes());
